I shall be communicating with students through announcements, exclusively v=
ia emails sent within CANVAS.

Please do not initiate multiple email threads unless explicitly asked to do=
 so.

Please write within exactly one thread; the penalty for starting new thread=
s is -1 points.

After one or two warnings I will not answer emails if they are not sent wit=
hin the initial thread.

This simple expedient makes it very easy to locate material.

One is required to read all announcements.

Exposition of the material requires a level of precission that far exceeds =
the precision needed in day-to-day discourse. In order to facilitate the ma=
stery of the required level of precission, I will consciously employ a regi=
ster that may be described as robotic; in other words, my communication may=
 seem computer-generated but it will not have the liberal doses of 'pleases=
 and thank-yous' characteristic of such communication, for instance, chat-g=
pt.

The above does not imply that I cannot interact in other, more familiar way=
s. But such registers will not be used in discussing course-material or req=
uirements. If I inadvertently sound like a human being, please point this o=
ut to me so that I may rectify this lapse on my part.

Of course, if one wishes to discuss something other than the course-materia=
l, then I will not employ the above mode of communication. It may take one =
some time to get used to this feature of the course. Please remember that c=
omputers are neither happy, nor sad, nor pleased, nor displeased, and canno=
t do much beyond distinguishing between correct and incorrect inputs by doi=
ng what it is told to do, or by giving an error message. A computer cannot =
praise, or blame, or flatter , or insult. This is exactly how I shall opera=
te.

It is useful, indeed imperative to remember these points when processing in=
formation in an announcement.

