tical-align:top; box-sizing:border-box; padding:20px;">
<p>I shall be communicating with students through announcements, exclusivel=
y via emails sent within CANVAS.</p>
<p><strong>Please do not initiate multiple email threads unless explicitly =
asked to do so.</strong></p>
<p><strong>Please write within exactly one thread; the penalty for starting=
 new threads is -1 points</strong>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>After one or two warnings I will not answer emails if they are not sent =
within the initial thread.</p>
<p>This simple expedient makes it very easy to locate material.&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>One is required to read all announcements</strong>.</p>
<p>Exposition of the material requires a level of precission that far excee=
ds the precision needed in day-to-day discourse. In order to facilitate the=
 mastery of the required level of precission, I will consciously employ a r=
egister that may be described as
 robotic; in other words, my communication may seem computer-generated but =
it will not have the liberal doses of 'pleases and thank-yous' characterist=
ic of such communication, for instance, chat-gpt.&nbsp;</p>
<p>The above does not imply that I cannot interact in other, more familiar =
ways. But such registers will not be used in discussing course-material or =
requirements. If I inadvertently sound like a human being, please point thi=
s out to me so that I may rectify
 this lapse on my part.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Of course, if one wishes to discuss something other than the course-mate=
rial, then I will not employ the above mode of communication. It may take o=
ne some time to get used to this feature of the course. Please remember tha=
t computers are neither happy, nor
 sad, nor pleased, nor displeased, and cannot do much beyond distinguishing=
 between correct and incorrect inputs by doing what it is told to do, or by=
 giving an error message. A computer cannot praise, or blame, or flatter , =
or insult.&nbsp;<span>This is exactly
 how I shall operate.</span><span>&nbsp;</span></p>
<p>It is useful, indeed imperative to remember these points when processing=
 information in an announcement.&nbsp;</p>
